Falsifies `socket_contract::verification::a_udp_bind_grant_admits_exactly_its_range`.

The defect: `udp_grant_allows` compares the port with `<` against the high bound, the off-by-one
a reader writes when it takes an inclusive range for a half-open one. A single-port UDP grant then
admits nothing, and every range loses its top port.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!` on `udp_grant_allows`, with the port equal to the
high bound.

diff --git a/crates/socket_contract/src/lib.rs b/crates/socket_contract/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/socket_contract/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/socket_contract/src/lib.rs
@@ -201,7 +201,7 @@
 pub const fn udp_grant_allows(grant: u64, port: u16) -> bool {
     let lo = ((grant >> 32) & 0xffff) as u16;
     let hi = ((grant >> 48) & 0xffff) as u16;
-    lo != 0 && port >= lo && port <= hi
+    lo != 0 && port >= lo && port < hi
 }
 
